      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we simplify the expression by distributing the subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(B+A)-(B-C)-A & =B+A-B+C-A \\\\  & =\\cancel{B}+\\cancel{A}-\\cancel{B}+C-\\cancel{A} \\\\  & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left with a single matrix. So, the result is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
